        itemId = 32862,
        name = "Violet Netherwing Drake",
        stepCount = 12,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Finish the Netherwing introduction and build Exalted reputation with dailies and repeatable egg turn-ins.\n\n1. Travel to Shadowmoon Valley in OUTLAND on a character able to fly. Enable Trivial Quests tracking and find Mordenai walking through Netherwing Fields around 60.0, 59.0; he may be fighting flayers, so use /targetexact Mordenai and look on the ground. For Kindness, kill Rocknail Flayers, combine their giblets into carcasses and feed 8 Mature Netherwing Drakes. If already Exalted, skip to step 10.\n\n2. Complete Seek Out Neltharaku, then Neltharaku's Tale. Neltharaku is a large dragon FLYING HIGH above the fields, patrolling roughly 58-70, 54-64. His map pin is a search point, not a stationary ground spawn. Follow his Infiltrating Dragonmaw Fortress quest and kill the required Dragonmaw orcs at the fortress around 69.0, 61.0.\n\n3. For To Netherwing Ledge!, fly to the island south of the mainland and collect 12 Nethervine Crystals from the quest sources there. Return to Neltharaku. For The Force of Neltharaku, use his enchanted crystal on enslaved Netherwing drakes at Dragonmaw Fortress, then help the freed drakes defeat their captors. Do not kill the drakes you are trying to rescue.\n\n4. Accept Karynaku and speak to the chained dragon on the fortress platform at 69.8, 61.5. Take Zuluhed the Whacked, defeat Zuluhed, loot his key and use it on Karynaku's chains. Complete her follow-up and Ally of the Netherwing with Mordenai. This finishes the introductory chain and provides the large reputation award.\n\n5. Continue Mordenai's Blood Oath of the Netherwing and In Service of the Illidari to Dragonmaw Base Camp on Netherwing Ledge. Let the Dragonmaw disguise apply, then speak to Overlord Mor'ghor at 66.2, 85.6 and Taskmaster Varkule Dragonbreath at 66.0, 86.4. These friendly quest NPCs are part of the disguise, for both Alliance and Horde.\n\n6. Speak to Yarzill the Merc at 66.0, 86.5 and complete Your Friend on the Inside. Find a Netherwing Egg and complete The Great Netherwing Egg Hunt; later eggs use Accepting All Eggs. The first hand-in normally gives 350 reputation and subsequent eggs 250 before bonuses. Egg hand-ins are repeatable without a daily cap.\n\n7. Search the ledge, floating rock shelves and Dragonmaw Fortress for lootable eggs. Also enter the Netherwing Mines at 65.3, 90.0: check corners and side passages for ground eggs and loot Nethermine Flayers, Ravagers and other lootable enemies for random egg drops. Murkblood Miners do not provide loot. Ground eggs are not available before the introductory unlock; do not spend hours searching for them on a character still before Ally of the Netherwing.\n\n8. Take the available dailies at the base camp and mine entrance while gathering eggs. For Netherwing Crystals, collect 30 crystals from ledge/mine enemies. At Friendly, mine quests include collecting 15 Nethermine Cargo and killing 15 Nethermine Flayers plus 5 Ravagers. These share the egg-farming area, so collect their objectives in the same run and return to the quest givers when complete.\n\n9. At each new reputation rank, return to the camp for promotion quests such as Rise, Overseer!, Stand Tall, Captain! and Hail, Commander! Keep repeating eggs and available dailies until Netherwing is Exalted. If a Burning Crusade Timewalking reputation bonus or another applicable reputation buff is active, use it for the introductory award and egg hand-ins; do not rely on another player's fixed egg count or completion time.\n\n10. At Exalted, take Bow to the Highlord from Taskmaster Varkule Dragonbreath at 66.0, 86.4, then Lord Illidan Stormrage from Overlord Mor'ghor at 66.2, 85.6. Stay for the event and Yarzill's rescue flight to Shattrath; allow the sequence to finish rather than flying to Shattrath before accepting the quests.\n\n11. Turn in to Barthamus in Shattrath's Lower City at 66.5, 16.8. Speak to Voranaku among the drakes beside him and complete that drake's quest for your free Violet Netherwing Drake. Only the first chosen color is free. If you already chose a different drake, use step 12 instead.\n\n12. For additional colors, return to Drake Dealer Hurlunk on Netherwing Ledge at 65.6, 86.0 while Exalted on this character. Buy Reins of the Violet Netherwing Drake for 200 gold if it is still missing, then use the reins. You can keep and learn all six colors; purchasing a second does not replace the first.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=32862",
        difficultyReason = "Finish the Netherwing introduction and build Exalted reputation with dailies and repeatable egg turn-ins.",
        difficulty = "medium",
    },
}

